      "body": "<!-- Thank you for your contribution! Please follow these guidelines to enhance your pull request. If anything is unclear, submit your PR and reach out to maintainers for assistance. Join our Slack community at https://slack.sglang.io to discuss further. -->\n\n<!-- PR title: [Type] scope: title, or [Type] [Hardware] scope: title.\nType: Feat, Fix, Refactor, Perf, Doc, Test, CI, or Chore.\nScope: any module or model name (no fixed list or letter-case restriction), e.g. attention, qwen3, or flash-attn.\nHardware: optional single tag without spaces. Use uppercase hardware tags (AMD, NVIDIA, NPU, MI300X), except for exactly these four spellings: Intel, Apple, Huawei, Ascend.\nTitle: no letter-case restriction.\nReverts: use GitHub's default title, Revert \"original title\".\nExamples: [Fix] attention: Fix KV cache indexing; [Perf] [AMD] flash-attn: Optimize decode performance. -->\n\nAssisted-by: OpenAI Codex\n\n## Motivation\n\nWhen a request finishes before its first Mamba tracking interval, the [int8-checkpoint path](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/6cac4dc3fe9a4bf15009f300132c3c7a1853c210/python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/unified_cache/components/mamba.py#L609-L627) reads an unwritten ping-pong state slot, then discards the zero-length checkpoint. The read is unnecessary; no output corruption was observed. Related [PR #44718](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44718) and [PR #39209](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/39209) address different checkpoint cases.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSkip the state read when tracked length is zero; nonempty checkpoints are unchanged. No user-facing documentation changes are needed.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Historical Qwen3.5-0.8B-Base HTTP warmup: the unwritten-state read disappeared after the fix.\n- On main `2e7c9d851c`, the focused checkpoint suite passed `2/2` with CPU-device and `datasets` stubs. On the fix branch, Qwen3.5-0.8B-Base served 21/21 HTTP requests on an RTX A6000 with int8 Mamba checkpoints enabled. This was a functional smoke test, not a KVGuard-instrumented read check; the local kernel-version guard was bypassed because `sglang-kernel` 0.4.5 is older than main requires.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nRTX A6000, Qwen3.5-0.8B-Base, int8 checkpoints: two warmed baseline/fix pairs of 80-request rounds at concurrency 8. Output throughput ranges (baseline vs. fix) overlapped for short requests (571–650 vs. 616–647 tok/s) and longer requests (492–526 vs. 454–524 tok/s); no consistent change was observed. An unrelated GPU job overlapped later rounds, so small differences need an exclusive-GPU rerun.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40847307069](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40847307069)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40847307011](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40847307011)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40847306840](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40847306840)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
